// Language section: Schema & Decorators.
page schema { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Schema & Decorators" {}

  text {
    span "Decorators (written `@name` or `@name(args)`) attach schema metadata to declarations and fields. Together they describe a document's legal structure, which `wcl check` validates." {}
  }

  h2 "Declaration decorators" {}

  table {
    rows:
      | "Decorator"          | "On"   | "Meaning" |
      | "`@document`"        | "type" | "Marks the document root schema (one per namespace)" |
      | "`@block(\"kind\")`" | "type" | "Makes the type a nestable block of that kind" |
      | "`@table(\"kind\")`" | "type" | "Row schema for pipe-table syntax" |
      | "`@schemaless`"      | "type" | "Opts a type out of root validation, allowing multiple decorators / reflection" |
  }

  h2 "Field decorators" {}

  table {
    rows:
      | "Decorator"            | "Meaning" |
      | "`@child(\"kind\")`"   | "A single nested block of the given kind" |
      | "`@children(\"kind\")`" | "A list of nested blocks (or union variants — dispatch)" |
      | "`@inline(slot)`"      | "Bind the block label to a field at that position" |
      | "`@default(expr)`"     | "Default value when the field is omitted" |
      | "`@connections(S)`"    | "Accumulate `->` connection statements as records" |
  }

  h2 "A worked example" {}

  text {
    span "A document root with one kind of child block, whose label becomes an inline field and whose port has a default:" {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
@block("service")
type Service {
  @inline(0)   name: utf8     // service "web" → name = "web"
  @default(80) port: u32
  region: utf8
}

@document
type Config {
  @children("service") services: list<Service>
}
WCL
  }

  text {
    span "Given that schema, this document validates: each `service` block contributes a `Service` to `services`, with `name` taken from the label and `port` defaulting to `80`." {}
  }
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
service "web" { region = "us-east-1" }
service "api" { port = 9090u32  region = "eu-west-1" }
WCL
  }

  callout "Reflection" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "decorator_names(T) and decorator_arg(T, name, slot) read decorators back at evaluation time — used by libraries (like wdoc) that dispatch on a block's declared kind."
  }

  text {
    span "Next: [Imports & Modules](imports)." {}
  }
}
